$ w --about

  ◆ tungsten · W · 74
  │ atomic mass    183.84 u
  │ density        19.3 g/cm³
  │ melting point  3421.85 °C
  │ boiling point  5554.85 °C
  │ state          solid
  │ category       transition metal
  │ discovered     1783
  │ named          From Swedish tung sten, 'heavy stone'. Its symbol W is from
  │   wolfram, after the ore wolframite: German wolf rahm, 'wolf's cream', from
  │   Agricola's Latin lupi spuma, 'wolf's froth', because the ore devoured tin
  │   during smelting as a wolf devours sheep.

  ◆ tungsten 0.2.0
  │ what      calculate with quantities and units, in words and math
  │ home      github.com/oddurs/tungsten
  │ data      CODATA 2022 (NIST), PubChem, NASA NSSDCA, USDA FoodData Central
  │ licence   MIT

